<title>BRAZIL: Bamerindus 9-mo loss 33.8 bln reais.</title>
<headline>Bamerindus 9-mo loss 33.8 bln reais.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's troubled Bamerindus, the country's third-largest bank, reported the following results for 1996's first nine months.</p>
<p>			Jan-Sept 1996	Jan-Sept 1995</p>
<p>    Net Loss	    33.799 million	   N/A</p>
<p>    Net Worth	   1.3 bln		N/A</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in Brazilian reais.</p>
<p>The bank, which released its financial results to Brazil's stock exchanges, said financial intermediation revenues totalled 2.364 billion reais, while financial intermediation gains reached 670.35 million reais.</p>
<p>-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 248 5413</p>
</text>
